 ],
 "synopsis": "Jio Platforms Ltd., the telecom and digital services arm of Reliance Industries Ltd., is reportedly seeking a valuation of about Rs 11 lakh crore ($114 billion) for its planned initial public offering. The company filed its draft prospectus in June for an offering of as many as 270 million new shares, equivalent to about 2.93% of its post-issue equity capital. The offering could open in the week of October 19 and list before October 30. Jio has appointed 19 banks to work on the share sale, including Kotak Mahindra Capital, Morgan Stanley, BofA Securities, Axis Capital, BNP Paribas, and Citigroup.",
